<div class="px-[15px] py-[15px] pb-[30px] border-t mt-[15px]" style="border-color: var(--border-primary);">
  <h3 class="text-[0.8rem] m-0 mb-2 font-bold" style="color: var(--text-primary);">About Battery Tool</h3>
  <p class="text-[0.7rem] leading-snug mb-2.5" style="color: var(--text-tertiary);">
    Battery Tool is a free, open-source 3D tool for designing custom lithium battery packs.
    Visualize Series/Parallel configurations (18650, 21700, LFP, Na-ion) in real-time.
  </p>
  <ul class="text-[0.7rem] pl-4 m-0 mb-2.5 leading-snug" style="color: var(--text-tertiary);">
    <li><strong>3D Visualization:</strong> Auto-generates spot-welding strips &amp; hex layouts.</li>
    <li><strong>Physics Engine:</strong> Simulates Voltage Sag, Joule Heating, and Efficiency losses.</li>
    <li><strong>Dynamic Runtime:</strong> Estimates runtime based on Constant Power/Current loads and SoC.</li>
    <li><strong>Chemistry Aware:</strong> Accurate curves for Li-ion, LiFePO4 (LFP), and LTO.</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="text-[0.65rem] mt-2" style="color: var(--text-muted);">Licensed under GPL v3</div>
</div>
